From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruiyangke <me@ry.ke>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] input: Use the Apple key bindings on iPadOS

Key bindings, shortcut hints and the monospace font were chosen with
`target_os = "macos"`. An iPad with a hardware keyboard uses Command and
Option shortcuts and shows them as symbols, so on iPadOS inputs got the
Windows and Linux bindings (Ctrl-based word and line deletion), `Kbd` drew
"ctrl-" hints, and the monospace family was one iPadOS doesn't have.

The bindings and `Kbd` now test `target_vendor = "apple"`, and the monospace
font Menlo is chosen for macOS and iOS. macOS behavior is unchanged.

Send upstream with an iPadOS port.
